//Line 1325:      //else if (strcmp(argv[1],"cldr_rect")==0) PolRelation=POL_CLDR_RECT;
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//Please remove commented lines completely (to keep the code clean). If you ever need them, they can be obtained from the repository.
//Also remove corresponding unused identifiers from const.h. In other words, it makes sense not only to use the same command line options for cubical and rectangular dipoles, but also the same internal identifiers.



Line 93: In my opinion, in this case, it only complicates the logic (precalc tables are building automaticaly)
Line 385: This trick can not be applied here. For sure now I calculate the number of elements in the array.
Line 1325: Done

[1]B.T. Draine 'Propagation of Electromagnetic Waves on a Rectangular Lattice of
